course: dictionary
lesson: 7709
title: A word about the mind
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: A psychologist is a person who studies the mind: how people think, feel and behave. In this word, mind means the thinking and feeling part of you. Psychologist is a noun, and its plural is psychologists.
explain: Read this: «The "10,000 hours" idea was made famous by the writer Malcolm Gladwell, based on research by the psychologist Anders Ericsson.» The word research is a clue. It tells you the psychologist studied something carefully, like a scientist testing and watching people.
explain: Some psychologists also help people. A school or educational psychologist may help pupils who find learning or feelings hard. Look at the word before psychologist: child psychologist, educational psychologist, sports psychologist. That first word tells you who or what the psychologist works with.
fact: A psychologist studies the mind and how people think, feel and behave.
fact: Some psychologists are trained to help people with worries, feelings or learning difficulties.
fact: Psychologist is a noun: one psychologist, two psychologists.
fact: Psychologists find that «lies often need more lies to protect them», so owning up early ends the web.
fact: The psychologist Daniel Wegner found that «trying hard not to think about something often makes it come back more», and he tested this with white bears.
exercise: «The "10,000 hours" idea was made famous by the writer Malcolm Gladwell, based on research by the psychologist Anders Ericsson.» What is a psychologist? | A type of school bell | A kind of doctor who only treats teeth | A person who sells and fixes bicycles | *A person who studies the mind and how people think, feel and behave
exercise: Which phrase names a psychologist who helps pupils with learning difficulties? | Kitchen psychologist | *Educational psychologist | Garden psychologist | Sports psychologist
exercise: «Owning up is scary for a minute and freeing afterwards.» Find and copy the word that means a short time. | afterwards | scary | *minute | freeing
test: Mia says a psychologist is a person who fixes cars. What is the best answer? | *No, a psychologist studies the mind and helps people with feelings, not cars | Yes, because the word has car in it | Yes, psychologists fix cars in their spare time | No, psychologists only work in shops
test: Which sentence uses psychologists correctly as a plural noun? | The psychologists is very kind and studies minds | Psychologist are a kind of bird | *Two psychologists wrote the report together | A psychologist wrote three reports and ran away
exam: Why do psychologists say owning up early is helpful, and what does the word psychologist mean? | Owning up is scary, so psychologists say never tell the truth | *A psychologist studies the mind, and owning up early ends the web of lies, so it is better than hiding | Psychologists say to hide the truth for as long as possible | A psychologist is a person who fixes machines, and owning up is a kind of game
